---
title: Cod kedgeree
category: Mains
cuisine: British
diet:
  - gluten-free
  - dairy-free
tags:
  - fish
servings: 2
difficulty: easy
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 30 minutes
created: 2026-05-20
updated: 2026-05-20
---

Place @cod fillets{250%g}(desalted) in an ovenproof baking dish and bake for ~{10%minutes} at 180°C until they are opaque and flaky.

Remove the cod from the oven and flake into small pieces, discarding any skin and bones.

In a #deep frying pan{}, heat @cumin seeds{2%tsp} and @mustard seeds{1%tsp} until they are fragrant.

> Optionally crush them in a mortar to release their flavours and return them to the pan.

Drizzle with @olive oil{}, add @onion{1}(finely chopped), @turmeric{2%tsp}(ground) and @chili flakes{1/2%tsp}, and sauté for ~{2%minutes}.

Add @white basmati rice{200%g} and @fish or vegetable broth{400%ml} to the pan. Add @salt{} as necessary.

Cover the pan with a lid and bring to a boil then reduce to a simmer, allowing it to cook for ~{10%minutes} with the lid on.

Once cooked, allow the rice to set for another ~{10%minutes} without removing the lid.

Soft boil @eggs{2} for ~{6%minutes} in a pan of water. Leave to cool.

Shell the eggs and quarter them. Fluff up the rice with a fork and fold everything together with the cod before serving. Season with @black pepper{}(crushed) and garnish with @parsley{}.
